          <div class="story-inner-text">
            <span class="story-tag-eyebrow">✦ THE STORY OF SWASTIC EXPORTS ✦</span>
            <h2 class="story-heading">A Legacy Born from Passion and Understanding</h2>
            <p class="story-description">
              <strong>Swastic Exports was born in 1980</strong> with a vision to create more than just a gemstone trading business — it was envisioned as a legacy built around trust, quality, and a deep understanding of natural gemstones.
            </p>
            <p class="story-description">
              The journey was initiated by <strong>Mr. Anil Tambi</strong>, who saw immense potential in Jaipur’s growing gemstone industry and believed that gemstones should be treated not merely as commodities, but as rare pieces of nature with individuality, character, and enduring value. His vision was to build relationships that would last generations — with jewellers, designers, and buyers who valued authenticity, quality, and reliability as much as the beauty of the stone itself.
            </p>
            <p class="story-description">
              Over time, that vision became the bedrock of Swastic Exports. What began as a family-led gemstone enterprise evolved into a world-class business dealing in fine emeralds, rubies, sapphires, and other precious gemstones, connecting Jaipur’s renowned gemstone lapidary expertise with an increasingly prestigious global clientele.
            </p>
            <p class="story-description">
              The next chapter of this remarkable journey has been carried forward by <strong>Ramsaran Tambi</strong> and <strong>Mohan Tambi</strong>, taking the family legacy forward while driving the company's evolution and meeting dynamic global gemstone demand.
            </p>
            <blockquote class="story-quote-box">
              “Gemstones are not merely commodities — they are rare pieces of nature with individuality, character, and enduring value.”
            </blockquote>
